In article <1993Aug9.154026.70955@cc.usu.edu>,  <sllfl@cc.usu.edu> wrote:
>	First, how the @#%^$$@# do you find enough food to stay alive?
>Invariably, I start out pretty good and get down to around level 5 or 6 only
>to starve to death.  I don't wear rings, and in fact, I don't see how anyone
>can wear rings and still stay alive.

	There are two things which you may not have considered.  One is that
it's no coincidence that corpses are represented by the same character as food
items.  Try eating those corpses while they're still fresh.  The other thing
is that when all else fails, #pray.  Your god may not do what you want him to,
but if the only other option is dying, you have little to lose.

>	Second, which characters are good, especially for starting out?  I was
>trying the knight, and two or three times my stats all periodically jumped
>(i.e. I became more intelligent, strong, etc).  Is this only a trait knights
>have or do all the characters benefit from this?

	For beginning players, I'd recommend a Priest and a Barbarian to
start.  The priest helps one to learn the importance of the blessed/cursed
nature of items, and the barbarian is just a straight-forward warrior type
that doesn't require any sort of subtlety to win.

>	Finally, there are a few items that I don't know how to use.  For
>example, what are the magic markers for?  An oracle mentioned something about
>engraving on the floor.  Do you use markers for this or not, and what good
>does it do?  How do you use rings?  For example, I was trying to use a ring
>of polymorph and I couldn't get it to work.  (I think I was trying to use the
>invoke command (M-i)).  What are you supposed to do with your pet?  Although
>it's better with 3.1.3 in that you can "displace" him now instead of waiting
>for him to move, again the oracle mentioned something about training your
>pet.  How is this possible?

	Okay...Magic markers can be used using either the a)pply command or
the E)ngrave command.  They're best used for writing on blank scrolls.
	Rings:  just p)ut it on and wait for it to kick in on its own.
	Pets:  In my experience, pets are useful three ways.  They will fight
other monsters for you (not always the ones you want them to,) they can help
you distinguish cursed items from non-cursed, and they can help you steal from
shops.

